  data:  # f30a
    kind: work_item  # f30a
    title: "Go analyzer records composite-literal field value (RunE: handler) as a calls edge — no call occurs at that site"  # f30a
    status: todo_hard  # f30a
    priority: 3  # f30a
    parent:  # f30a
    tags:  # f30a
    - go  # f30a
    - analyzer  # f30a
    - taint  # f30a
    isbefore: []  # f30a
    duplicate_of: []  # f30a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f30a
    pr_ref:  # f30a
    description: "Found while building INV-zuhig's Go-side control (PR #367): the Go analyzer\nrecords `RunE: runServe` inside an INSTANCE-form composite literal\n(`cmd := &cobra.Command{RunE: runServe}`) as a `calls` edge from the enclosing\nfunction — but no call happens at that line; it is a function-value\nassignment. The package-level form (`var rootCmd = &cobra.Command{...}`)\nemits no such edge, which is how the asymmetry surfaced. Consequences, both\ndirections: (a) recall blessing — this over-claim is why cobra handlers in\nthe instance form minted taint sources all along, masking the\ndispatch-edges-invisible-to-taint gap that INV-zuhig closed; (b) precision\ncost — a `calls` edge asserts an invocation that does not occur at that\nsite, which pollutes anything that trusts edge semantics (slice explanations\nname a call that is really a registration). With go_cobra + the taint change\nnow covering BOTH literal forms via dispatches_to, the analyzer edge could be\ndemoted to `references` without losing minting — but ONLY after verifying on\nthe go corpus that nothing else leans on it (dead-code BFS, slice quality).\nFile first, demote after measurement; do not assume the fix direction."  # f30a
    fields: {}  # f30a
- op: discuss  # 9b7c
  at: '2026-10-01T10:31:25Z'  # 9b7c
  by: agent  # 9b7c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9b7c
  clock: 2  # 9b7c
  nonce: 9b7c  # 9b7c
  message: "BEARS ON THIS ITEM (from WI-bivin-ronup-kuzam-giliz-sinoz-gihug-tigas-rovom, branch jgstern-agent/fix/bivin-go-bare-package-scope, commits ddc8438f45 + 30c09f1398, NOT merged): the keyed_element arm that emits these struct_field_reference calls edges now resolves a BARE identifier value (Command{RunE: run}) only in the caller's own package, skips a name bound in the enclosing declaration, and never binds a method or field. Over 8 corpus repos (analyze_go, dev 7a645c6c76 vs branch) struct_field_reference edges changed: 180 cross-package binds and 34 own-package binds removed (sampled: prometheus testFloatHistogram / Replace, alertmanager: 83 binds of a local variable named now to the method Log.now in another package), 1 same-target rebind. The SELECTOR form (Command{RunE: pkg.Run}) is unchanged and is filed separately as WI-kibah-kasus-timun-risuk-kilam-birid-dugok-dakuh. This item's question -- whether a field value should be a calls edge at all -- is untouched."  # 9b7c
- op: discuss  # 3ada
  at: '2026-11-01T10:55:34Z'  # 3ada
  by: agent  # 3ada
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3ada
  clock: 3  # 3ada
  nonce: 3ada  # 3ada
  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/taint3/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. Core claim reproduces: newServe's cmd := &cobra.Command{RunE: runServe} emits calls newServe->runServe (evidence struct_field_reference) beside the cobra linker's dispatches_to. The asymmetry is gone: the package-level var rootCmd = &cobra.Command{RunE: runRoot} now also emits calls rootCmd(variable)->runRoot. Scope has widened: META-mino (62212c8cd7, 2026-10-29) routes unkeyed slice elements and local bindings through the same _emit_value_reference, so f := handler and []func(){other} also emit calls (function_reference). WI-bivin/WI-kibah only changed which target binds; the edge-type question is open. MECHANISM: value-position function reference emitted as edge_type calls (struct_field_reference / function_reference) instead of references. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-kibah,WI-bivin."  # 3ada
