    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. Core claim reproduces: newServe's cmd := &cobra.Command{RunE: runServe} emits calls newServe->runServe (evidence struct_field_reference) beside the cobra linker's dispatches_to. The asymmetry is gone: the package-level var rootCmd = &cobra.Command{RunE: runRoot} now also emits calls rootCmd(variable)->runRoot. Scope has widened: META-mino (62212c8cd7, 2026-10-29) routes unkeyed slice elements and local bindings through the same _emit_value_reference, so f := handler and []func(){other} also emit calls (function_reference). WI-bivin/WI-kibah only changed which target binds; the edge-type question is open. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFound while building INV-zuhig's Go-side control (PR #367): the Go analyzer\nrecords `RunE: runServe` inside an INSTANCE-form composite literal\n(`cmd := &cobra.Command{RunE: runServe}`) as a `calls` edge from the enclosing\nfunction — but no call happens at that line; it is a function-value\nassignment. The package-level form (`var rootCmd = &cobra.Command{...}`)\nemits no such edge, which is how the asymmetry surfaced. Consequences, both\ndirections: (a) recall blessing — this over-claim is why cobra handlers in\nthe instance form minted taint sources all along, masking the\ndispatch-edges-invisible-to-taint gap that INV-zuhig closed; (b) precision\ncost — a `calls` edge asserts an invocation that does not occur at that\nsite, which pollutes anything that trusts edge semantics (slice explanations\nname a call that is really a registration). With go_cobra + the taint change\nnow covering BOTH literal forms via dispatches_to, the analyzer edge could be\ndemoted to `references` without losing minting — but ONLY after verifying on\nthe go corpus that nothing else leans on it (dead-code BFS, slice quality).\nFile first, demote after measurement; do not assume the fix direction."  # 7fa4
